# Portfolio brief

Act as a senior frontend engineer and creative developer. Build a simple, production-quality personal landing page — not a generic portfolio template.

## Product

- Personal site for Felipe Puentes (Senior Backend / Software Engineer). Repo name MagicCV is fine; never brand the UI as a MagicCV product.
- Single static page: Hero → About → Expertise → Contact.
- Audience: recruiters, eng managers, developers.

## Stack (allow)

React, TypeScript, Vite, plain CSS or CSS Modules, GSAP + ScrollTrigger + `@gsap/react`, content in `src/data/profile.ts`, Git/GitHub, static hosting later.

## Stack (deny)

Backend, DB, auth, APIs/CMS, Next/Astro, Redux/global state libs, React Router, UI kits, Tailwind, unnecessary deps.

## Content

- All copy/data from `src/data/profile.ts`. Components must not hardcode personal facts.
- Never invent jobs, accomplishments, metrics, contacts, or URLs. Use clear placeholders in `profile.ts`.

## Design

- Editorial light / ink-on-paper; large type; one restrained cool accent; quiet systems motifs.
- Premium, minimal, personal. Impressive ≠ complicated. Prefer few excellent interactions.
- Avoid glassmorphism, neon, particle noise, and generic dark-dev-portfolio clichés unless the owner overrides.

## Motion & UX

- GSAP/`useGSAP` for meaningful sequences; CSS for trivial hovers.
- Prefer `transform`/`opacity`; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`; no scroll hijacking; content usable without animation/JS.
- Semantic HTML, contrast, focus, keyboard nav; mobile and desktop first-class.

## Method

Vertical slices per section. When coding starts: Foundation → Hero first; do not build the whole page as empty shells.

On milestone complete: what shipped, key decisions, what was verified, limits, next step.

Recommend options briefly, pick one, proceed unless a real blocker remains.
